_:c14n74 a claimchain:PaperAssessment ;
	claimchain:key_limitations "Latent distance is not symmetry-reduced and also encodes measurement conditions (LIM2, LIM3), contradicting the distance-metric criterion (CLAIM1c)." , "Three maps, two alloys, one crystal structure, one encoder; generality claims exceed this scope (CLAIM5, CLAIM9)." , "Threshold selection rests on an assumed WCSS elbow and ad hoc constants (ASM2, METH4)." , "Validation by agreement with conventional EBSD cannot fail: disagreements are read as higher sensitivity (CLAIM4)." ;
	claimchain:missing_evidence "Boundary precision/recall and a contrast-to-noise metric." , "Data beyond FCC Ni-base alloys and a single detector; released code." , "Independent ground truth (HR-EBSD, ECCI, TEM or synthetic patterns) for extra domains and substructure." , "Quantitative test of latent distance against misorientation and dislocation density." , "Reconstruction error and compression ratio." ;
	claimchain:overall_validity "PARTIAL" ;
	claimchain:summary "Clear concept and well-described tools that reproduce conventional EBSD trends on three FCC Ni-base maps. The central gene claim is argued rather than shown, the distance criterion is contradicted by the paper's own limitations, and \"finer detail\" and \"better contrast\" are judged by eye without ground truth." .
